# CODEOWNERS
#
# Syntax: each line is a path pattern followed by one or more owners.
# Owners may be GitHub usernames (@user), teams (@org/team), or email addresses.
# The last matching rule takes precedence, so more specific rules come last.

# NOTE: @your-name and @dsh-upstream are PLACEHOLDERS. Replace them with the real
# maintainer handles before the repository is published.

# Default owner for the whole repository (fallback for anything not covered below).
* @your-name

# rin asset layer — the project's own code (rin/ is the only writable layer).
rin/** @your-name

# dsh upstream code (packages/, apps/, docs/, vendor/, python/, native/).
# These currently fall back to the default owner above. When an upstream dsh
# maintainer is named, uncomment and fill in their handle:
# packages/** @dsh-upstream
# apps/**     @dsh-upstream
# docs/**     @dsh-upstream
# vendor/**   @dsh-upstream
# python/**   @dsh-upstream
# native/**   @dsh-upstream
